# =============================================================================
# Native Codex API-key authentication (optional).
#
#   cp config/codex.env.example config/codex.env   # then edit config/codex.env
#
# Codex owns authentication. Either set the standard CODEX_API_KEY below for
# usage-based API access, or leave this file absent and run
# `bin/codex login --device-auth` for ChatGPT subscription access.
#
# This file is gitignored (only *.example is committed). NEVER commit a real key.
# `scripts/env.sh` sources it first in the config chain, so every line must be
# valid shell. Leave the placeholder commented until it is replaced.
# =============================================================================

#CODEX_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
